{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>But those who hope in YHWH shall renew [strength].</b> Before the first strength is exhausted, another strength will come to them from HaShem. Similarly: though it be cut down, it will yet sprout anew (Job 14:7). And this expression is close to the language of Kedar:" "<b>They shall mount up [with] wing.</b> Like 'Who will give me a wing' (Psalms 55:7). And it is possible this is the meaning: for Israel, who hoped, HaShem will strengthen them and restore them to Jerusalem, and the Babylonians, who are mighty, will be weakened:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "Resolved יי as YHWH per standard divine-name convention; the lemma reads וקוי יי יחליפו (Isaiah 40:31)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:17.897055372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}